        "id": 7616,
        "name": "DevoDog",
        "username": "DevoDog",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/d/bbce88/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2013-04-07T14:37:40.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Played SotM for the first time yesterday.</p><p>My dad was playing Absolute Zero and had Focused Apertures (Increase cold damage dealt by Absolute Zero by 1) and Null-Point Calibration Unit (When Absolute Zero would take cold damage, he regains that many HP instead). We had Cramped Quarters Combat in play (Change the type of all damage to melee damage....)</p><p>He wanted to use AZ's power (AZ deals himself 1 fire damage or cold damage).</p><p>What we're unclear on is:</p><p>1. Does the +1 cold damage take effect? (We weren't really sure on this one.)</p><p>2.&nbsp;Does he heal from this?&nbsp; (We thought NO since it was converted to melee damage.)</p><p>PS. I bought this game a couple of weeks back, but only got a chance to play it yesterday. Really wish I had bought this one instead of Legacy many months back. SotM was a lot of fun and I really felt like I was actually doing something instead of just playing my cards \"in the right order.\"</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:37:56.752Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
